  </p>

  <h2>Brands we do <em>not</em> promise—and “Other” rows</h2>
  <p>
    You will notice an <strong>Other</strong> label in many lanes. That is intentional taxonomy debt: sellers ship unbranded blanks, unlabeled factory runs, or meme-tier items that do not deserve a luxury string.
    We keep those rows rather than forcing a fake logo, because honest filtering beats aesthetic SEO.
  </p>
  <p>
    We also do <strong>not</strong> maintain a complete list of every trademark on Chinese marketplaces—only what our curators have ingested into the public English mirror.
    If a brand is missing, it usually means no stable seller link passed moderation yet, not that the factory cannot produce it.
  </p>

